{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b76a-3db9-7643-9fed-985cd96a2982","session_id":"01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6","message":{"id":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01_8RAC0LmyvqiYCRwnZtqe4663","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\006\\scripts\\check-no-collab.mjs"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":97285,"output_tokens":228,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":94080,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","_messageId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","traceparent":"00-ca409312e57460dad670bff2ccb3f3ff-0161882b422c291a-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T19:09:15.578Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b76a-3dbc-7716-ae18-258737be8c78","session_id":"01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_5xducJCSnNmzKprlgUTn9594","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→#!/usr/bin/env node\n   2→// Frozen-file check: the registered characterization/golden files must keep their exact bytes.\n   3→// Hashing normalizes CRLF to LF so an autocrlf checkout and a Linux CI checkout agree.\n   4→import crypto from 'node:crypto'\n   5→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   6→import path from 'node:path'\n   7→import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n   8→\n   9→const HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\n  10→const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(HERE, '..')\n  11→\n  12→const MANIFEST = ['test', 'characterization', 'frozen-files.json']\n  13→const COPY_DIR = 'test/fixtures/characterization/v0.1/'\n  14→const STABLE = 'test/characterization/stable.test.mjs'\n  15→const SOURCE_COMMIT = 'f75bb76'\n  16→const FORBIDDEN_PREFIXES = ['lib/', 'bin/', 'config/']\n  17→const ALLOWED_PREFIXES = [COPY_DIR, 'contracts/spec/', 'contracts/golden/']\n  18→\n  19→const USAGE = 'usage: node scripts/check-frozen-files.mjs [--root <dir>]'\n  20→\n  21→/** Bytes as text with every CRLF folded to LF, so the digest is line-ending agnostic. */\n  22→export function normalizeContent(buffer) {\n  23→  return buffer.toString('latin1').replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n')\n  24→}\n  25→\n  26→export function contentHash(buffer) {\n  27→  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(normalizeContent(buffer), 'latin1').digest('hex')\n  28→}\n  29→\n  30→function isAllowed(rel) {\n  31→  if (rel === STABLE) return true\n  32→  return ALLOWED_PREFIXES.some((prefix) => rel.startsWith(prefix) && rel.length > prefix.length)\n  33→}\n  34→\n  35→/** Reject anything that is not a plain repository-relative posix path inside the allowed set. */\n  36→export function classifyPath(rel) {\n  37→  if (rel.includes('\\\\')) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: rel }\n  38→  if (/^[A-Za-z]:/.test(rel)) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: rel }\n  39→  if (path.posix.isAbsolute(rel)) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: rel }\n  40→  if (rel.split('/').includes('..')) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: rel }\n  41→\n  42→  const normalized = path.posix.normalize(rel)\n  43→  if (normalized === '.' || normalized === '' || normalized.startsWith('../')) {\n  44→    return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: rel }\n  45→  }\n  46→\n  47→  const lowered = normalized.toLowerCase()\n  48→  for (const prefix of FORBIDDEN_PREFIXES) {\n  49→    if (lowered === prefix.slice(0, -1) || lowered.startsWith(prefix)) {\n  50→      return { id: 'frozen.forbidden_path', detail: normalized }\n  51→    }\n  52→  }\n  53→  if (!isAllowed(normalized)) return { id: 'frozen.outside_allowed', detail: normalized }\n  54→  return { path: normalized }\n  55→}\n  56→\n  57→function walkFiles(dir, prefix, found) {\n  58→  let entries\n  59→  try {\n  60→    entries = fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })\n  61→  } catch {\n  62→    return\n  63→  }\n  64→  for (const entry of entries) {\n  65→    const rel = prefix === '' ? entry.name : `${prefix}/${entry.name}`\n  66→    if (entry.isDirectory()) walkFiles(path.join(dir, entry.name), rel, found)\n  67→    else if (entry.isFile()) found.push(rel)\n  68→  }\n  69→}\n  70→\n  71→export function checkFrozenFiles({ root }) {\n  72→  const errors = []\n  73→  const base = path.resolve(root)\n  74→  const manifestFile = path.join(base, ...MANIFEST)\n  75→\n  76→  let manifest = null\n  77→  try {\n  78→    manifest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(manifestFile, 'utf8'))\n  79→  } catch {\n  80→    errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_missing', detail: 'test/characterization/frozen-files.json' })\n  81→    return { errors, count: 0 }\n  82→  }\n  83→\n  84→  if (!manifest || typeof manifest !== 'object' || Array.isArray(manifest)) {\n  85→    errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: 'manifest must be a JSON object' })\n  86→    return { errors, count: 0 }\n  87→  }\n  88→  if (manifest.source_commit !== SOURCE_COMMIT) {\n  89→    errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: `source_commit must be ${SOURCE_COMMIT}` })\n  90→  }\n  91→  if (!Array.isArray(manifest.files)) {\n  92→    errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: 'files must be an array' })\n  93→    return { errors, count: 0 }\n  94→  }\n  95→\n  96→  const seen = new Set()\n  97→  const registered = new Set()\n  98→  let count = 0\n  99→\n 100→  for (const entry of manifest.files) {\n 101→    if (!entry || typeof entry !== 'object' || Array.isArray(entry)) {\n 102→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: 'every registered file must be an object' })\n 103→      continue\n 104→    }\n 105→    const rel = entry.path\n 106→    if (typeof rel !== 'string' || rel === '') {\n 107→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: 'registered file needs a non-empty path' })\n 108→      continue\n 109→    }\n 110→    if (typeof entry.sha256 !== 'string' || !/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(entry.sha256)) {\n 111→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: `${rel} has an invalid sha256` })\n 112→      continue\n 113→    }\n 114→    if (seen.has(rel)) {\n 115→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.manifest_schema', detail: `duplicate path ${rel}` })\n 116→      continue\n 117→    }\n 118→    seen.add(rel)\n 119→\n 120→    const verdict = classifyPath(rel)\n 121→    if (verdict.id) {\n 122→      errors.push({ id: verdict.id, detail: verdict.detail })\n 123→      continue\n 124→    }\n 125→    registered.add(verdict.path)\n 126→    count += 1\n 127→\n 128→    let buffer = null\n 129→    try {\n 130→      buffer = fs.readFileSync(path.join(base, ...verdict.path.split('/')))\n 131→    } catch {\n 132→      buffer = null\n 133→    }\n 134→    if (buffer === null) {\n 135→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.file_missing', detail: verdict.path })\n 136→      continue\n 137→    }\n 138→    if (contentHash(buffer) !== entry.sha256) {\n 139→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.hash_mismatch', detail: verdict.path })\n 140→    }\n 141→  }\n 142→\n 143→  const copyFiles = []\n 144→  walkFiles(path.join(base, ...COPY_DIR.split('/').filter(Boolean)), '', copyFiles)\n 145→  for (const rel of copyFiles.sort()) {\n 146→    if (!registered.has(`${COPY_DIR}${rel}`)) {\n 147→      errors.push({ id: 'frozen.unregistered', detail: `${COPY_DIR}${rel}` })\n 148→    }\n 149→  }\n 150→  if (!registered.has(STABLE)) {\n 151→    errors.push({ id: 'frozen.unregistered', detail: STABLE })\n 152→  }\n 153→\n 154→  return { errors, count }\n 155→}\n 156→\n 157→function main() {\n 158→  const args = process.argv.slice(2)\n 159→  let root = REPO_ROOT\n 160→\n 161→  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i += 1) {\n 162→    const flag = args[i]\n 163→    if (flag === '--root') {\n 164→      const value = args[i + 1]\n 165→      if (typeof value !== 'string' || value === '') {\n 166→        process.stderr.write(`--root requires a directory\\n${USAGE}\\n`)\n 167→        process.exitCode = 2\n 168→        return\n 169→      }\n 170→      root = path.resolve(value)\n 171→      i += 1\n 172→    } else {\n 173→      process.stderr.write(`unknown argument: ${flag}\\n${USAGE}\\n`)\n 174→      process.exitCode = 2\n 175→      return\n 176→    }\n 177→  }\n 178→\n 179→  const { errors, count } = checkFrozenFiles({ root })\n 180→  if (errors.length === 0) {\n 181→    process.stdout.write(`check-frozen-files: ok (${count} files)\\n`)\n 182→    process.exitCode = 0\n 183→    return\n 184→  }\n 185→  for (const error of errors) process.stdout.write(`FAIL ${error.id} ${error.detail}\\n`)\n 186→  process.stdout.write(`check-frozen-files: FAILED (${errors.length} errors)\\n`)\n 187→  process.exitCode = 1\n 188→}\n 189→\n 190→const invokedDirectly =\n 191→  process.argv[1] && path.resolve(process.argv[1]).toLowerCase() === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url).toLowerCase()\n 192→\n 193→if (invokedDirectly) main()\n 194→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","_messageId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","traceparent":"00-ca409312e57460dad670bff2ccb3f3ff-0161882b422c291a-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T19:09:15.581Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b76a-3dc1-74a2-b013-c58453a20f75","session_id":"01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_01_8RAC0LmyvqiYCRwnZtqe4663","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→#!/usr/bin/env node\n   2→// Fails when any repository file refers to the blueprint working directory.\n   3→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   4→import path from 'node:path'\n   5→import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n   6→\n   7→const HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\n   8→const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(HERE, '..')\n   9→const SCAN_DIRS = ['lib', 'scripts', 'test', 'contracts', 'docs']\n  10→const SKIP_NAMES = new Set(['node_modules', '.git'])\n  11→const FIXTURE_PREFIX = 'test/fixtures/no-collab/'\n  12→const USAGE = 'usage: node scripts/check-no-collab.mjs [--root <dir>]'\n  13→\n  14→// Built by concatenation so this file does not match itself.\n  15→const NEEDLE = ['.', 'coll', 'ab'].join('')\n  16→\n  17→function toPosix(value) {\n  18→  return value.split(path.sep).join('/')\n  19→}\n  20→\n  21→function byCodePoint(a, b) {\n  22→  if (a < b) return -1\n  23→  if (a > b) return 1\n  24→  return 0\n  25→}\n  26→\n  27→function walk(dir, base, out) {\n  28→  let entries\n  29→  try {\n  30→    entries = fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })\n  31→  } catch {\n  32→    return\n  33→  }\n  34→  for (const entry of entries) {\n  35→    if (SKIP_NAMES.has(entry.name)) continue\n  36→    const full = path.join(dir, entry.name)\n  37→    if (entry.isDirectory()) walk(full, base, out)\n  38→    else if (entry.isFile()) out.push(toPosix(path.relative(base, full)))\n  39→  }\n  40→}\n  41→\n  42→function listFiles(root, skipFixture) {\n  43→  const found = []\n  44→  if (fs.existsSync(path.join(root, 'package.json'))) found.push('package.json')\n  45→  for (const dir of SCAN_DIRS) walk(path.join(root, dir), root, found)\n  46→  const unique = [...new Set(found)].sort(byCodePoint)\n  47→  if (!skipFixture) return unique\n  48→  return unique.filter((rel) => !rel.startsWith(FIXTURE_PREFIX))\n  49→}\n  50→\n  51→function main(argv) {\n  52→  let root = REPO_ROOT\n  53→  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {\n  54→    const flag = argv[i]\n  55→    if (flag === '--root') {\n  56→      const value = argv[i + 1]\n  57→      if (typeof value !== 'string' || value === '') {\n  58→        process.stderr.write(`check-no-collab: --root requires a directory\\n${USAGE}\\n`)\n  59→        process.exitCode = 2\n  60→        return\n  61→      }\n  62→      root = path.resolve(value)\n  63→      i += 1\n  64→    } else {\n  65→      process.stderr.write(`check-no-collab: unknown argument: ${flag}\\n${USAGE}\\n`)\n  66→      process.exitCode = 2\n  67→      return\n  68→    }\n  69→  }\n  70→\n  71→  const files = listFiles(root, true)\n  72→  const violations = []\n  73→\n  74→  for (const rel of files) {\n  75→    let text\n  76→    try {\n  77→      text = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, rel), 'utf8')\n  78→    } catch {\n  79→      continue\n  80→    }\n  81→    const lines = text.split(/\\r?\\n/)\n  82→    for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i += 1) {\n  83→      if (lines[i].toLowerCase().includes(NEEDLE)) violations.push({ rel, line: i + 1 })\n  84→    }\n  85→  }\n  86→\n  87→  if (violations.length > 0) {\n  88→    violations.sort((a, b) => byCodePoint(a.rel, b.rel) || a.line - b.line)\n  89→    for (const hit of violations) process.stdout.write(`FAIL no_collab ${hit.rel}:${hit.line}\\n`)\n  90→    process.stdout.write(`check-no-collab: FAILED (${violations.length} violations)\\n`)\n  91→    process.exitCode = 1\n  92→    return\n  93→  }\n  94→\n  95→  process.stdout.write(`check-no-collab: ok (scanned ${files.length} files)\\n`)\n  96→  process.exitCode = 0\n  97→}\n  98→\n  99→const invokedDirectly =\n 100→  process.argv[1] &&\n 101→  path.resolve(process.argv[1]).toLowerCase() === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url).toLowerCase()\n 102→\n 103→if (invokedDirectly) main(process.argv.slice(2))\n 104→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","_messageId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b76a35b37e37bbb9866c60567051","traceparent":"00-ca409312e57460dad670bff2ccb3f3ff-0161882b422c291a-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T19:09:15.586Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b76a-3d91-7b3b-b2c3-a7b0680a3d70","session_id":"01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6","message":{"id":"01a1b76a3d917b3bb2c3a7aec22cf5ff","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"check-no-collab: our new files must not contain \".collab\" — fine.\n\ncheck-test-discovery: let's check quickly. And check-contract-doc, check-ci — these probably don't touch our files but check-fast runs them. They pass at baseline presumably.\n\nLet me check check-test-discovery for orphan requirements (test files must be in enumerated dirs — unit and characterization are enumerated). Fine.\n\nNow let me look at lib/select.mjs and lib/commands to see old forecast usage — but we keep old function untouched. Just ensure no naming conflicts.\n\nAlso I need to check interfaces §6 for pool shape `used_fraction` with `at`, `reading`. Design covers.\n\nLet me now design the implementation carefully.\n\n### lib/pools.mjs\n\nExports: round3, billedTokens, normalizeQuota, resolveResetAt, evaluatePools, remainingForModels.\n\n```js\nconst DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT = 0\n\nexport function round3(value) {\n  const n = Number(value)\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return value\n  const abs = Math.abs(n)\n  const scaled = Number((abs * 1000).toPrecision(15))\n  const rounded = Math.round(scaled) / 1000\n  const signed = n < 0 ? -rounded : rounded\n  return signed + 0   // eliminate -0\n}\n```\nCheck: round3(0.0625) → abs*1000 = 62.5 → toPrecision(15) \"62.5000000000000\" → 62.5 → round 63 → .063. Good. 0.1875 → 187.5 → 188 → .188 ✓. -0.0625 → -0.063 ✓. 1.2344 → 1234.4 → 1234 → 1.234 ✓. 0 → 0 ✓. -0.0004: abs*1000 = 0.4 → round 0 → 0/1000 = 0, n<0 → -0 → +0 → 0 ✓. Object.is(0,0) true; Object.is(-0,0) false, and `+0` converts -0 to 0? `(-0) + 0` = 0 (positive zero) — yes, -0 + 0 = +0. Good.\n\nAlso `2 * (1 - 0.33333)` = 1.33334 → round3 → 1.333 ✓; 10*(1-0.33333)=6.6667 → 6.667 ✓.\n\nNon-finite returns value as-is: `return value` (original) per \"非有限数原样返回\".\n\n`billedTokens(row, w)`:\n```js\nexport function billedTokens(row, cache_read_weight = 0) {\n  if (!row || typeof row !== 'object') return 0\n  if (Number.isFinite(row.tokens)) return row.tokens\n  const w = Number.isFinite(cache_read_weight) ? cache_read_weight : 0\n  const input = num(row.input_tokens)\n  ...\n  return input + output + cache_write + w * cache_read\n}\n```\nNote \"行上有有限数字 tokens 时直接用\". If tokens is a numeric string? Design says \"有有限数字 tokens\". Use typeof number check? `Number.isFinite(row.tokens)` returns false for string. Tests use numbers. I'll be a bit lenient: use Number(row.tokens) if finite? Design says finite number. Hmm, \"数值字符串先 Number()\" only mentioned for normalizeQuota. For billedTokens, \"行上有有限数字 tokens 时直接用;否则...\" I'll accept numbers only via Number.isFinite(row.tokens) but also handle null. Actually being lenient with Number() is harmless... but could break if tokens is null → Number(null)=0 finite → returns 0 instead of falling back. Better strict.\n\n`normalizeQuota(quota)`:\n```js\nexport function normalizeQuota(quota) {\n  const q = quota && typeof quota === 'object' ? quota : {}\n  let remaining_fraction = null\n  let remaining_mtok = null\n  let remaining_usd = null\n  let reason = null\n  const pct = toFinite(q.remaining_pct)\n  if (pct !== null) remaining_fraction = clamp(pct / 100, 0, 1)\n  const remaining = toFinite(q.remaining)\n  const unit = typeof q.unit === 'string' ? q.unit : null\n  if (remaining !== null && unit === 'credits') {\n    const rate = toFinite(q.credits_per_mtok)\n    if (rate !== null && rate > 0) remaining_mtok = remaining / rate\n    else if (remaining === 0) remaining_mtok = 0\n    else reason = 'credits_conversion_missing'\n  } else if (remaining !== null && unit === 'tokens') {\n    remaining_mtok = remaining / 1e6\n  }\n  const usd = toFinite(q.remaining_usd)\n  if (usd !== null) remaining_usd = usd\n  const anyKnown = remaining_fraction !== null || remaining_mtok !== null || remaining_usd !== null\n  if (!anyKnown && reason === null) reason = 'capacity_unknown'\n  return { remaining_fraction, remaining_mtok, remaining_usd, reason }\n}\n```\nCheck golden cases:\n- q-pct-5: fraction .05, mtok null, usd null, reason null. buildForecast reason: tasks_left null & not only-usd → 'no_samples'. ✓\n- q-credits-zero: remaining 0 credits, remaining_mtok 0, reason null. status known. tasks_left_assumed = floor(0/0.5)=0. risk: classifyRisk tasks_left null basis none fraction null → unknown; then zero-remaining rule: remaining_mtok===0 → exhausted, risk_basis none. Golden expects risk exhausted ✓.\n- q-credits-rate: 1/1000 = 0.001 mtok ✓.\n- q-tokens: 2 ✓.\n- q-usd: remaining_usd 3, tasks_left floor(3/0.5)=6, basis usd, risk ok.\n- q-pct-0: fraction 0. classifyRisk with fraction 0 → exhausted (fraction table <=0 exhausted) ✓. risk_basis 'fraction'.\n- q-pct-4: 0.04 < 0.05 → critical ✓.\n- q-pct-15: 0.15 → not <0.15 → ok ✓.\n- q-credits-no-rate: remaining_mtok null, fraction null → status unknown, risk unknown, basis none, reason credits_conversion_missing. Note reason from normalizeQuota. ✓ golden expects reason credits_conversion_missing, risk unknown, basis none.\n\nBut careful about reason in buildForecast for unknown: \"unknown 时取剩余量阶段给出的原因\". So use `remaining.reason` if status unknown. For `{}` → capacity_unknown ✓.\n\nCareful: q-credits-rate has reason null, tasks_left 0 → risk tasks exhausted. But also zero-remaining rule not triggered (mtok 0.001). classifyRisk: tasks_left 0 basis tasks → exhausted ✓.\n\nNow `resolveResetAt({cli, config, window, rows, now})`:\n- parse helper `parseTime(v)`: if number finite → v; if string → Date.parse; else NaN. Note `Date.parse` returns number. `new Date(ms).toISOString()`.\n- cli first, then config, then rolling window.\n- window.anchor === 'rolling' && window.length_s > 0: candidates rows whose at in (now - length*1000, now]. Take earliest at. reset = earliest + length*1000.\n- Return { reset_at: ISO|null, reset_source }.\n\nNote the function receives `now`, must validate finite? design says functions with `now` param throw TypeError when not finite; \"签名里有 now 的函数只收显式传入的毫秒数...now 不是有限数字时抛 TypeError\". resolveResetAt and evaluatePools and buildForecast take now. So assertFiniteNow.\n\nBut careful: acceptance A-15 calls resolveResetAt with now always. buildForecast throws TypeError for NaN. Also buildForecast without now? `buildForecast({ now: Number.NaN })` throws TypeError. What should buildForecast({}) do — no now → throw TypeError too. Design says now 必填. Fine.\n\nAlso etaExhaust takes now; should throw TypeError if non-finite? It's in \"签名里有 now 的函数\". Yes, add assert. But acceptance A-10 calls etaExhaust with Date.parse(...) fine.\n\nHmm wait: `resolveResetAt` might be called with `window` undefined. Handle.\n\n`evaluatePools({ models, pools, rows, now, reading_ttl_s, cache_read_weight })`:\n\nSteps per design §3.5.\n\nPool shape: `{ id, window: { start_at, reset_at, reset_source, anchor, length_s }, capacity_mtok: { model: number | {value} }, reading: { value, at } | null, used_fraction: { value, at } | null }`.\n\ncapacityOf(pool, model): cap = pool.capacity_mtok?.[model]; if number finite → it; if object with finite `value` → value; else null.\n\npools that list model: for each pool where capacityOf(...) !== null.\n\nEffective reset per pool: derive cli/config from window:\n```\nif (window.reset_source === 'cli') cli = window.reset_at\nelse if (window.reset_source === 'config' || window.reset_source == null) config = window.reset_at  // only if reset_at present\n```\nCareful: \"来源为 estimated 或 unknown 时丢弃存量值\". If reset_source is undefined but reset_at present → config. If reset_at absent → no candidates.\n\nThen resolveResetAt({ cli, config, window, rows, now }). Note: when window.reset_source === 'estimated' with reset_at present, we pass window to resolveResetAt which may estimate from rolling (needs anchor/length_s). Golden cases have window without reset_source and with reset_at → config, reset_at normalized \"2026-11-07T12:00:00.000Z\" ✓ (input \"…T12:00:00Z\").\n\nstart_at: window.start_at parse → start base. Effective start for window filtering: \"窗口内（start_at <= at <= now，起点用步骤 1 的有效起点）\". Step 1 defines effective window start changes to reset_ms for cli-crossed. Otherwise start_at.\n\nHmm: \"若 `reset_source === 'cli'` 且 `now >= reset_ms`：该池的有效窗口起点改为 `reset_ms`，早于 `reset_ms` 的读数视为作废、早于 `reset_ms` 的行不计。\"\n\nReading freshness: reading exists, not invalidated, and now - reading.at <= ttl*1000. Need reading.at parse finite.\n\nused_p:\n- fresh reading: reading.value + Σ over rows with at > reading.at && at <= now of tokens_i/(cap_i * 1e6).\n- else: rows with start <= at <= now summed.\n- \"没有窗口且存在需要计入的行 → unknown(window_unknown)\": if effective start is null (no start_at and no cli reset) and there are rows to include (passing at <= now filter) → unknown.\n\nWait, for b44 cases window.start_at exists. What about \"窗口\" meaning start boundary. If start is null and rows exist in the relevant selection → window_unknown.\n\n- If any participating row's model has no capacity in pool p → unknown(ledger_capacity_unknown).\n\nNote in b44-unknown-capacity-row: rows [{model:'codex:gpt-x', tokens:1000}] and pool has opus/sonnet only. Model queried: opus and sonnet. The row participates (in window, no fresh reading) → cap missing → unknown for both. ✓\n\nFor b44-ledger-sonnet-1m: opus capacity 2, sonnet 10; row sonnet 1M tokens. used_p for pool is shared across models? Yes, used_p is per pool (the pool has single reading of used fraction). So used = 1/(10*1e6)=0.1. remaining for sonnet = 10*(1-0.1)=9; opus = 2*0.9=1.8 ✓. Note for opus, the row model sonnet has capacity → defined, so no unknown. Good.\n\nb44-reading-then-1m: reading 0.5 at 09:55, row at 09:58 → used = 0.5 + 0.1 = 0.6 → sonnet 10*0.4=4 (round3 4.000000000000001→4) ✓, opus 2*0.4=0.8 ✓. Note 2*(1-0.6)=0.8000000000000002 → round3 → 0.8 ✓.\n\nb44-fresh-reading-ignores-earlier-rows: row at 08:00 < reading.at 09:55 → not counted → 0.5.\n\nb44-stale-reading-uses-ledger: reading at 09:00, now 10:00 → age 3600s > 600 → stale → ledger rows in window → 0.1 → 9 / 1.8 ✓. reason null (fresh? no). status known.\n\nb44-rounding: reading 0.33333 → opus 2*0.66667=1.33334 → 1.333; sonnet 10*0.66667=6.6667 → 6.667 ✓.\n\nb44-two-pools-min: pool5h sonnet cap10 reading .5 → 5; pool7d cap20 reading .1 → 18; min 5 ✓. remaining_fraction = min(0.5, 0.9) = 0.5.\n\nModel result: if any member pool unknown → unknown with that reason; no pools → unknown(capacity_unknown); else known, remaining_mtok round3(min). remaining_fraction round3(min fraction). reason null.\n\nModel pools detail: `pools[i] = { pool_id, remaining_mtok, remaining_fraction, used_fraction, used_mtok, reset_at, reset_in_h, reset_source, recheck }`. For unknown pools, what are remaining_mtok etc.? Design doesn't say precisely; forecast output uses evaluatePools details only when status known (burn/eta). For unknown we can set nulls. I'll set remaining_mtok null, remaining_fraction = 1-used? Hmm. Let's think: for `remainingForModels` only status/remaining_mtok/reason matter.\n\nFor buildForecast pool six-field output, when status unknown... §3.9: burn/eta only when known. §3.10: pools output each six fields. For unknown model, what to output for remaining_mtok? Probably null. I'll produce pools with remaining_mtok null when pool unknown, remaining_fraction null, and used_fraction maybe null.\n\nFor model with no pools at all (empty pools input) → forecast pools []. \n\nLet me keep detail for known pools fully computed; for unknown pools: `{ pool_id, remaining_mtok: null, remaining_fraction: null, used_fraction: null, used_mtok: null, reset_at: resolved reset ISO, reset_in_h: computed, reset_source, recheck }`.\n\nHmm, but for `unknown` model with pools, forecast pools output six fields with nulls — schema allows null.\n\nNow `used_mtok = cap_p(m) * used_p` (per model). `reset_in_h = max(0, round3((reset_ms - now)/3600000))`, null if no reset time. `recheck` true only when source !== 'cli' && now >= reset_ms.\n\nImportant: `reset_at` in detail = ISO from resolveResetAt (normalized). reset_source likewise.\n\nNow the reset behavior for cli crossed: effective start = reset_ms, reading invalidated (since reading.at < reset_ms presumably), rows before reset_ms excluded. If reading.at >= reset_ms it'd be fresh. Fine: \"早于 reset_ms 的读数视为作废\" — condition reading.at >= reset_ms (and <= now).\n\nCareful with AC-019 fixture: reading.at = 11:50:01, reset 12:00:00. Before: now 11:59:59 < reset → normal; reading age 598s ≤ 600 → fresh → 0.5, recheck false. After advance 2000: now 12:00:01 ≥ reset and source cli → invalidate reading (11:50:01 < 12:00), effective start 12:00:00, no rows → used 0 → used_fraction 0 ✓, recheck false ✓.\n\nconfig version: source config, now >= reset → recheck true, no change: reading still fresh? age = now - 11:50:01 = 600s exactly at now=12:00:01 → 600000 ms <= 600*1000 ✓ fresh → 0.5 ✓.\n\nNow, row parsing: `at` ISO string. For b44 rows use `tokens`.\n\n\"没有窗口且存在需要计入的行\" — define startMs = effective start (from start_at or cli reset). If startMs === null: rows with at <= now are \"需要计入\" → if any exist → window_unknown. If none → used 0 (no rows).\n\nAlso need to handle unknown capacity check for rows participating. For fresh-reading path, participating rows are those with at > reading.at && at <= now; rows before reading not participating (b44-fresh-reading-ignores-earlier-rows: row is sonnet, has capacity anyway).\n\nEdge: rows with unparsable at → skip.\n\nNow what about `rows` for models other than queried? All rows count toward pool usage regardless of model, as long as capacity known. Yes.\n\n`billedTokens` uses cache_read_weight default 0. In evaluatePools, pass options.cache_read_weight ?? 0.\n\nA-7: row `{ model:'s', input_tokens:1000000, cache_read_tokens:1000000, at }`; pool window start 07:00 reset 12:00, capacity s:10, reading null. w=0 → tokens 1e6 → used 1e6/1e7 = 0.1 → remaining 9 ✓. w=1 → 2e6 → 0.2 → 8 ✓.\n\nNow `remainingForModels` = projection `{ [model]: { status, remaining_mtok, reason } }`. A-6 compares whole object to `c.expected`, deep equal. Object key order doesn't matter for deepStrictEqual.\n\n### lib/forecast.mjs\n\nMust keep: DEFAULT_PRICES, normalizePrices, estimateCost, forecast() (deprecated). Must contain `systemNow` exactly twice: import line `import { systemNow } from './context.mjs'` — that's 1 occurrence; default param `now = systemNow()` — 2nd. No other mention. And no `Date.now` anywhere (comments too? The check is substring on whole file: `forecast.includes('Date.now')`. So don't write \"Date.now\" in comments!). Also pools.mjs must not contain \"systemNow\" etc.\n\nNote acceptance R-3 checks `pools.includes('setTimeout')` etc. Avoid.\n\nNow the engine:\n\n```js\nimport { systemNow } from './context.mjs'\nimport { normalizeQuota, evaluatePools, round3 } from './pools.mjs'\n```\nWait design says `export { round3 } from './pools.mjs'` in forecast.mjs. Use:\n```js\nimport { normalizeQuota, evaluatePools } from './pools.mjs'\nexport { round3 } from './pools.mjs'\n```\nBut we also need round3 internally for burn_per_task etc. We can import round3 and also re-export:\n```js\nimport { round3, normalizeQuota, evaluatePools } from './pools.mjs'\nexport { round3 }\n```\nThat's a re-export of imported binding — allowed: `export { round3 }` after import. Good.\n\nDEFAULT_POLICY:\n```js\nexport const DEFAULT_POLICY = {\n  reading_ttl_s: 600,\n  cache_read_weight: 0,\n  usage_estimate_mtok: { Heavy: 2, Normal: 0.5, Light: 0.1 },\n}\n```\n\nquantileForUsage(samples, usage):\n```js\nconst USAGE_P = { Heavy: 0.9, Normal: 0.5, Light: 0.25 }\nexport function quantileForUsage(samples, usage) {\n  const values = Array.isArray(samples) ? samples.filter((x) => Number.isFinite(x)).slice() : []\n  const n = values.length\n  if (n < 3) return null\n  const p = USAGE_P[usage] ?? USAGE_P.Normal\n  values.sort((a, b) => a - b)\n  return values[Math.ceil(p * n) - 1]\n}\n```\nCheck n12 heavy: ceil(0.9*12)=ceil(10.8)=11 → sorted[10]=11 ✓. n20 heavy: ceil(18)=18 → sorted[17]=18 ✓. n20 normal: ceil(10)=10 → 10 ✓. n20 light: ceil(5)=5 → 5 ✓. n12 normal: 6 ✓; light ceil(3)=3 → 3 ✓. n4 heavy: ceil(3.6)=4 → 0.4 ✓; normal ceil(2)=2 → 0.2 ✓; light ceil(1)=1 → 0.1 ✓. n3 heavy ceil(2.7)=3 → 0.3 ✓ normal ceil(1.5)=2 → 0.2 ✓ light ceil(0.75)=1 → 0.1 ✓.\n\n\"只取有限数字\" — filter non-finite. Golden inputs are plain numbers.\n\nconfidenceFor(n, cv):\n```js\nexport function confidenceFor(n, cv) {\n  const count = Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0\n  if (count <= 0) return 'none'\n  if (count < 5) return 'low'\n  if (count < 20) return 'medium'\n  return Number.isFinite(cv) && cv > 1 ? 'medium' : 'high'\n}\n```\n✓ n3-cv5 → low.\n\nclassifyRisk({tasks_left, tasks_left_basis, remaining_fraction}):\n```js\nexport function classifyRisk({ tasks_left = null, tasks_left_basis = 'none', remaining_fraction = null } = {}) {\n  if (Number.isFinite(tasks_left) && (tasks_left_basis === 'tasks' || tasks_left_basis === 'usd')) {\n    const risk = tasks_left <= 0 ? 'exhausted' : tasks_left <= 2 ? 'critical' : tasks_left <= 5 ? 'low_reserve' : 'ok'\n    return { risk, risk_basis: tasks_left_basis }\n  }\n  if (Number.isFinite(remaining_fraction)) {\n    const risk = remaining_fraction <= 0 ? 'exhausted' : remaining_fraction < 0.05 ? 'critical' : remaining_fraction < 0.15 ? 'low_reserve' : 'ok'\n    return { risk, risk_basis: 'fraction' }\n  }\n  return { risk: 'unknown', risk_basis: 'none' }\n}\n```\nCheck frac-0.15: 0.15 < 0.15 false → ok ✓ (0.15 double is 0.1499999999999999944..., and literal 0.15 same value, so comparison false). ✓\n\nburnMtokPerHour({used_mtok, hours_since_window_start}):\n```js\nexport function burnMtokPerHour({ used_mtok = 0, hours_since_window_start = 0 } = {}) {\n  const used = Number.isFinite(used_mtok) ? used_mtok : 0\n  const hours = Number.isFinite(hours_since_window_start) ? hours_since_window_start : 0\n  return round3(used / Math.max(hours, 1 / 60))\n}\n```\nCheck burn-clamp-zero-hours: 0.3/(1/60)=18.000000000000004 → round3 18 ✓. burn-clamp-tiny: 1/max(0.001, 0.016667)= 60 → 60 ✓. burn-5.5-over-5h: 1.1 (1.1 exactly? 5.5/5 = 1.1, 1.1*1000=1100.0000000000002? toPrecision 15 → 1100 → 1.1) ✓. burn-rounding: 2/3=0.6666666 → 666.6666 → 667 → .667 ✓. zero used → 0 ✓.\n\nHmm non-finite used: if used null → treat 0? Not tested. Design: `round3(used_mtok / max(hours, 1/60))`.\n\netaExhaust({now, remaining_mtok, burn_mtok_per_hour, reset_at}):\n```js\nexport function etaExhaust({ now, remaining_mtok, burn_mtok_per_hour, reset_at = null } = {}) {\n  const nowMs = assertNow(now)\n  const remaining = Number.isFinite(remaining_mtok) ? remaining_mtok : 0  // hmm\n  ...\n}\n```\nCareful: if remaining_mtok not finite? Not tested. Keep: if not finite → maybe null? Let's follow: `remaining_mtok <= 0 → eta = now`. If NaN comparisons false. I'll treat non-finite remaining as 0? Risky but untested. Use `const remaining = Number.isFinite(remaining_mtok) ? remaining_mtok : 0`.\nHmm, if remaining is 0 and burn > 0 → eta = now, exhausts = now < reset → true (eta-empty expects true) ✓.\n\nburn finite and > 0:\n```\neta = now + Math.round(remaining / burn * 3600000)\n```\nCheck eta-after-reset: 5/2*3600000 = 9000000 → 12:30 ✓ exhausts 12:30 < 12:00? false ✓.\neta-equal-reset: 1/0.5=2h → 12:00, strict < → false ✓.\n\neta_exhaust_at = new Date(eta).toISOString(); need `.000Z` — toISOString always does ms.\nreset_at → parse; if null → exhausts_before_reset null. else eta < resetMs.\nReturn exactly `{ eta_exhaust_at, exhausts_before_reset }`.\n\nOrder of checks: `remaining <= 0` → eta = now. Else if burn <= 0 or non-finite → eta null. Else compute.\n\neta null and remaining > 0 → exhausts false. eta null and remaining <=0? Can't happen (remaining<=0 gives eta=now). Design: \"`eta_exhaust_at` 为 null 且剩余 > 0 → `false`\". So when eta null → exhausts false (if reset null → still null? \"reset_at 为 null → null\" takes priority). Order: if reset null → null; else if eta null → false; else eta < reset.\n\nHmm with remaining<=0 and reset null → null. Fine.\n\n### buildForecast\n\nSignature: `buildForecast({ model = '', quota = null, pools, rows = [], samples, usage = 'Normal', now, policy } = {})`.\n\nassertNow(now) throws TypeError if not finite.\n\npolicy merge: shallow merge over DEFAULT_POLICY; usage_estimate_mtok merge too? \"policy 参数浅合并在其上\" — shallow. So if policy provides usage_estimate_mtok it replaces whole object. I'll do `{ ...DEFAULT_POLICY, ...policy }` but then a partial usage_estimate_mtok would break. Design says shallow; do shallow but guard usage_estimate_mtok lookup with fallback to DEFAULT_POLICY. Simpler: \n```js\nconst merged = { ...DEFAULT_POLICY, ...(policy && typeof policy === 'object' ? policy : {}) }\nconst estimates = { ...DEFAULT_POLICY.usage_estimate_mtok, ...(merged.usage_estimate_mtok || {}) }\nmerged.usage_estimate_mtok = estimates\n```\nHmm that's deep-ish merge. Design says shallow merge on top of defaults. I'll just do shallow and then when reading estimate: `const est = merged.usage_estimate_mtok?.[usage] ?? DEFAULT_POLICY.usage_estimate_mtok[usage]`. Fine.\n\n1. 剩余量:\n```js\nconst poolList = Array.isArray(pools) ? pools : []\nlet remaining = null\nif (poolList.length > 0) {\n  const evaluated = evaluatePools({ models: [model], pools: poolList, rows, now, reading_ttl_s: merged.reading_ttl_s, cache_read_weight: merged.cache_read_weight })[model]\n  remaining = evaluated ? { remaining_mtok: evaluated.remaining_mtok, remaining_fraction: evaluated.remaining_fraction, remaining_usd: null, reason: evaluated.reason, status: evaluated.status } : { null... }\n}\nif (!remaining) remaining = normalizeQuota(quota)\nelse if quota?.remaining_usd finite → remaining_usd = that\n```\nHmm design: \"两者都给时以 pools 为准，且 quota.remaining_usd 仍可作为 usd 剩余量.\" So when pools given: remaining_mtok/fraction from pools, remaining_usd from quota if present.\n\nBut what about pools path where evaluated unknown (status unknown)? Then remaining_mtok null, remaining_fraction null, reason ledger_capacity_unknown. remaining_usd might still be present. status: known if any non-null.\n\nWait: what if pools are provided but the model has no pools? evaluatePools returns unknown(capacity_unknown) for that model. Then quota would be ignored... Design: \"pools 非空 → evaluatePools(...)[model]；否则 → normalizeQuota(quota)\". So yes, quota ignored except remaining_usd. When pools non-empty but model not listed → unknown capacity_unknown. OK.\n\nHmm, but AC-015 A-2 calls buildForecast without pools → normalizeQuota. Fine.\n\nAlso evaluatePools could return undefined for model? It always returns entry for each requested model. OK.\n\nI need used_fraction and pool details for burn/eta. Let me have buildForecast compute `const evaluated = evaluatePools(...)` when pools non-empty, keep it.\n\n2. samples: token sequence and cost sequence.\n```js\nconst list = Array.isArray(samples) ? samples : []\nconst tokenValues = list.map(s => s && Number.isFinite(s.mtok) ? s.mtok : null).filter(v => v !== null)\n```\nHmm \"mtok 为有限数的样本形成 token 序列\". Note values could be numeric strings? Design says finite; use Number.isFinite(s.mtok).\n\ntokens_per_task = { p25: quantileForUsage(tokenValues,'Light'), p50: ...'Normal', p90: ...'Heavy', n: tokenValues.length }.\n\n3. tasks_left: q = quantile for usage from tokenValues (or cost values for usd).\n`const q = quantileForUsage(tokenValues, usage)`; if remaining_mtok !== null && q !== null && q > 0 → floor(remaining_mtok/q), basis tasks.\nelse costQ = quantileForUsage(costValues, usage); if remaining_usd !== null && costQ !== null && costQ > 0 → floor(usd/costQ), basis usd.\nelse null, 'none'.\n\nNote \"取用户 usage 对应分位数 q，q > 0\".\n\nfloor negative → clamp 0 later (\"写出的 tasks_left 只允许 null 或 ≥0\").\n\nq-credits-rate: mtok 0.001, q for Normal = 0.2 → floor(0.005)=0 ✓ tasks. Good.\n\n4. tasks_left_assumed: if tasks_left === null && remaining_mtok !== null: floor(remaining_mtok / est). est could be 0/undefined → guard: if finite and > 0 else null.\n\nFor { remaining_pct:50, remaining:2000000, unit:'tokens' }: fraction .5, mtok 2, no samples → tasks_left null, assumed floor(2/0.5)=4 ✓.\n\n5. risk: classifyRisk({tasks_left, tasks_left_basis, remaining_fraction}) — note remaining_fraction must be the raw (or rounded?) value. Design §3.5 says classify uses unrounded fraction; buildForecast remaining_fraction output rounded. Use unrounded for classify. For 0.05 from 5/100 → exactly 0.05 (5/100 = 0.05 double equals literal). ✓\n\nZero-remaining rule: if risk unknown && (remaining_mtok === 0 || remaining_usd === 0) → exhausted/basis none.\n\nThen clamp tasks_left negative to 0.\n\n6. confidence: n = list.length. cv from the sequence used for tasks_left: if basis 'tasks' → tokenValues; if 'usd' → costValues; if 'none' → null? \"cv 取参与 tasks_left 的那条序列；tasks_left 为 null、序列长度 < 2 或均值等于 0 时为 null\". So if tasks_left null → cv null.\n\n```js\nfunction cvOf(values) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(values) || values.length < 2) return null\n  const mean = values.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/values.length\n  if (mean === 0) return null\n  const variance = values.reduce((a,b)=>a+(b-mean)**2,0)/values.length\n  return Math.sqrt(variance)/mean\n}\n```\n20 samples 19×1, 1×100: mean = (19+100)/20 = 5.95; variance = (19*(1-5.95)^2 + (100-5.95)^2)/20 = (19*24.5025 + 8845.2025)/20 = (465.5475+8845.2025)/20=9310.75/20=465.5375; sqrt=21.576; /5.95=3.626 >1 → medium ✓ (n=20).\nflat 20×1: cv=0 → high ✓.\n\nconfidence = confidenceFor(list.length, cv).\n\nNote AC-015 A-2 golden q-cases: samples [] → n=0 → none. Fine (not asserted).\n\n7. status: known if any of remaining_mtok/fraction/usd non-null else unknown; if unknown → risk unknown basis none.\n\nNote: for q-credits-no-rate: all null → unknown, risk unknown ✓.\n\n8. reason:\n- unknown → remaining.reason (from normalize/evaluate). For {} → capacity_unknown ✓.\n- known: if tasks_left === null && only usd remaining (i.e., remaining_usd !== null && remaining_mtok === null && remaining_fraction === null?) → 'usd_samples_missing'. Design: \"有效样本不足（tasks_left === null）且只有 usd 剩余量 → usd_samples_missing，其余样本不足 → no_samples\". \"只有 usd 剩余量\" = remaining_mtok null && remaining_fraction null && remaining_usd non-null.\n- tasks_left non-null → null.\n\nCheck q-pct-5: known (fraction .05), tasks_left null, not only usd → no_samples ✓ (not asserted).\nq-usd: tasks_left 6 → reason null.\nAC-016 A-8: no samples, mtok 5 → reason no_samples ✓.\nAC-018 {remaining:1,credits}: status unknown → reason credits_conversion_missing ✓.\n\nHmm, what if known via usd alone and tasks_left computed? reason null.\n\n9. burn/eta only when pools path && status known:\nFind pool detail with minimum remaining_mtok among evaluated[model].pools. \"取该模型剩余量最小的池，并列时取 pools 输入顺序中的第一个\". Use evaluated pools array order.\n\nBut pools detail remaining_mtok are round3 values; min on those. For b44-reading-half sonnet: 5 and ... only one pool.\n\nburn: used_mtok (cap*used_p, unrounded) and hours_since_window_start = (now - effectiveStartMs)/3600000. Need effective start exposed. Design §3.9 says \"hours_since_window_start: (now - 有效窗口起点)/3600000\". So evaluatePools detail should carry window start. Not in the six-field output but internal detail can include extra. But design §3.5 specifies pools[i] fields exactly listed and says used_* and recheck don't enter forecast output. It says `pools[i] = { pool_id, remaining_mtok, ..., recheck }` — exact keys? It's specified as that object. Adding extra `start_at` might violate \"不要自行发明字段\"? For internal detail, adding fields could be considered inventing. Hmm. But A-15 only checks used_fraction & recheck; A-8 checks forecast pools six fields.\n\nAlternative: buildForecast computes effective start itself by re-deriving. But duplication. Alternatively evaluatePools detail can include `window_start_at`... The design's list looks authoritative (\"pools[i] = {...}\"). Yet burn needs window start. §3.9 says hours_since_window_start = (now - 有效窗口起点)/3600000. We can compute the effective start in buildForecast from the pool object: use the same resolution logic. That requires re-implementing reset resolution — but we can export a helper? Not in export list. Hmm.\n\nOption: evaluatePools returns an extra internal field `_window_start_ms` (non-enumerable?). Non-enumerable property won't appear in deepStrictEqual? Actually assert.deepStrictEqual compares own enumerable properties. Non-enumerable props are ignored. That's a clean trick but hacky.\n\nBetter: buildForecast can call evaluatePools and also compute per-pool effective start using a small internal function in forecast.mjs? That duplicates logic and risks divergence.\n\nAlternative: compute hours since window start in forecast from `pool.window.start_at` directly — but cli-crossed reset changes start. For the tested case (A-8), start_at = 07:00, now 10:00 → 3h, used_mtok = 10*0.5 = 5 → burn = 5/3 = 1.666... → round3 1.667 ✓. That matches. But correctness for cli-crossed case would be off (should use reset_ms). To be correct, I can expose an internal helper from pools.mjs that's not in the design's export list... \"不要自行发明任何字段、版本号或章节名\" — about fields/names; adding an extra helper export may be acceptable? Design says \"另有：lib/pools.mjs：...\" listing functions. Adding an extra export is inventing API. Safer: attach the effective start as a non-enumerable property? Or use a Symbol? Hmm.\n\nCleanest within spec: in evaluatePools detail, include `used_fraction`, `used_mtok`, and also compute `reset_at`. For hours_since_window_start, forecast can derive start as: if reset_at (resolved) and source cli and now >= reset → start = reset; else window.start_at. That's exactly the rule from §3.5 step 1, and can be implemented locally in a tiny helper inside forecast.mjs (a few lines), or... Actually simpler: pools detail could include `hours_since_window_start`? That's an extra field again.\n\nI think a tiny local helper `windowStartMs(pool, now, resetInfo)` in forecast.mjs is acceptable and not an \"invented field\". But design says burn formula takes hours_since_window_start from \"有效窗口起点\". Implementing the derivation in forecast duplicates 3 lines. But duplication risk minimal.\n\nAlternatively: make evaluatePools detail include `used_mtok` (already) and `window_start_at` — extra field would show up in deepStrictEqual only if compared; A-15 compares only used_fraction/recheck. Golden b44 uses remainingForModels projection. Forecast pools slice six fields. So an extra field is invisible everywhere. But \"pools[i] = {...}\" exact spec — adding a field contradicts spec text slightly. Acceptance doesn't test it. Hmm. The risk of failing acceptance is zero either way; the risk of a reviewer complaining is small.\n\nI'll go with a non-enumerable property? That's weird. Let me instead have `evaluatePools` include only spec fields and in `buildForecast` derive effective start with a small local function that mirrors §3.5 step 1 (using resolved reset_at/reset_source already present in pool detail). That uses only spec fields:\n\n```js\nfunction effectiveWindowStartMs(pool, detail, now) {\n  const window = pool && pool.window && typeof pool.window === 'object' ? pool.window : null\n  const start = window ? parseMs(window.start_at) : null\n  if (detail.reset_source === 'cli' && detail.reset_at !== null) {\n    const resetMs = Date.parse(detail.reset_at)\n    if (now >= resetMs) return resetMs\n  }\n  return start\n}\n```\nAnd hours = (now - start)/3600000 if start finite; else null.\n\nIf start null → burn null? Design doesn't specify; set burn/eta null in that case? Hmm. For pools path with no start_at, maybe window_unknown already. I'll compute hours = start !== null ? (now-start)/3600000 : 0 → burn huge. Better: if start null, burn = null and eta null. Not tested.\n\nAlso when used_mtok is 0 → burn 0 → eta nu