\n\n**test/unit/pools.test.mjs**:\n```js\nimport test from 'node:test'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport fs from 'node:fs'\nimport { normalizeQuota, remainingForModels } from '../../lib/pools.mjs'\nimport { buildForecast } from '../../lib/forecast.mjs'\n\nconst shapes = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(new URL('../../contracts/golden/quota-shapes.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'))\nfor (const c of shapes.cases) {\n  test(`[AC-015] ${c.id}`, () => {\n    const actual = buildForecast({ quota: c.input.quota, samples: c.input.samples, usage: c.input.usage, now: 0 })\n    for (const key of Object.keys(c.expected)) assert.deepStrictEqual(actual[key], c.expected[key], `${c.id} ${key}`)\n  })\n}\ntest('[AC-015] golden case count', () => { assert.equal(shapes.cases.length, 9) })\n// plus normalizeQuota direct tests\n```\nWait — golden file read at module scope uses fs; check-seams only scans lib. Fine.\n\nBut careful: buildForecast with samples [] and no pools; now 0. requireNow(0) fine.\n\nDirect tests for normalizeQuota five shapes (design §4): \"normalizeQuota 五种形状直测\" — five shapes: pct, credits (rate / no rate / zero), tokens, usd, none. Write a couple of tests with [AC-015] tags? They must be tagged in a file; tags only need to exist. Extra tests fine. But names must not create duplicate title issues. I'll name `[AC-015] normalizeQuota percentage`, etc.\n\nCareful: A-1 checks output contains ids; extra fine.\n\nb44 cases:\n```js\nfor (const c of b44.cases) {\n  test(`[AC-016] ${c.id}`, () => {\n    const actual = remainingForModels({ models: c.input.models, pools: c.input.pools, rows: c.input.rows, now: Date.parse(c.input.now), reading_ttl_s: c.input.reading_ttl_s })\n    assert.deepStrictEqual(actual, c.expected, c.id)\n  })\n}\ntest('[AC-016] golden case count', () => assert.equal(b44.cases.length, 9))\n```\n\n**test/unit/forecast-engine.test.mjs**: [AC-017]\n- Load four golden files; dispatch table by fn.\n- Test titles `[AC-017] <case.id>` for every case ac