{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b76b-6c13-71ea-af12-7cf63340071e","session_id":"01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6","message":{"id":"01a1b76b6c1371eaaf127cf4d7dce799","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, no references.\n\nNow, let's check lib/select.mjs and commands using forecast — just to be safe that adding exports doesn't break (it can't).\n\nNow let me double-check AC-016 A-7 first part: pool has `used_fraction: {value:0.5, at:'2026-11-07T09:55:00Z'}` and no `reading`. window has no `reset_source`. capacity value `{value:10}`. → remaining 5. Our capacity reader handles object. Reading detection: no `reading` → check `used_fraction` object with finite value → use it. ✓\n\nA-7 second: pool `reading: null` explicit → no reading. Rows count.\n\nNow `remaining_fraction` in remainingForModels? It's a projection excluding it. Fine.\n\nLet me double check b44 `b44-used-0`: no reading, rows [], start 07:00, now 10:00 → used 0 → remaining 2 and 10 ✓.\n\nNow about `now` validation in evaluatePools: Date.parse(c.input.now) finite ✓.\n\nNow design §3.5 says used_p clamped [0,1]. For reading 0.5 + row 0.6 = 1.1 → 1. Fine.\n\nNow a subtle point: for models where pool has capacity but another model in capacity... irrelevant.\n\nAnother subtlety: in b44-unknown-capacity-row, we compute used for pool once per model; but used_p is per pool, not per model — computed identically. Fine.\n\nImplementation approach in evaluatePools: for each model, for each pool listing model, compute pool state. To avoid recomputation, precompute a map pool.id → evaluation per pool (independent of model except used_mtok). But pool details include remaining per model, so per (model,pool). The used_p/unknown is per pool. I'll compute pool usage once (cache by pool index).\n\nPool state: { used (number|null), unknownReason (string|null), startMs, resetAt, resetSource, resetMs, recheck, capByModel }.\n\nFor rows participating: need cap for each row model → if undefined → unknownReason 'ledger_capacity_unknown'.\n\nEdge: \"参与求和的行里，只要某行的模型在池 p 的 capacity_mtok 里没有容量\" — for fresh reading path, participating rows only.\n\nDetermine participation: rows filtered by at > reading.at (fresh) or start <= at <= now. Then capacity check.\n\nWait: for fresh reading, rows before reading.at are excluded from both sum and capacity check ✓.\n\nAlso rows with at > now excluded.\n\nWhat about rows with model whose capacity is 0? \"没有容量\" means key absent. capacity 0 → division by 0 → Infinity. Hmm. Treat capacity null (absent or non-finite) as missing. Value 0 is finite... division by zero → Infinity used. Let's treat cap <= 0 as missing? Design says \"没有容量\". Edge untested. I'll guard: if cap is not finite → missing. If cap is 0 → used becomes Infinity → clamp 1. Eh. Keep simple: require finite; 0 yields Infinity → clamp to 1. Fine but ugly. I'll treat `cap === 0` as unknown too? No—\"没有容量\" = absent key. I'll require finite number > 0 to add, else unknown. Actually if cap is 0 and row exists, capacity genuinely 0 → division undefined. I'll mark unknown with ledger_capacity_unknown when cap is non-finite or <= 0. Not tested; safe.\n\nHmm, but capacity 0 pool with no rows: remaining 0 → fine. Only for participating rows.\n\nNow window_unknown: when startMs null and there are rows with at <= now. For fresh reading with start null: rows after reading — does window_unknown apply? \"没有窗口且存在需要计入的行 → 该池 unknown(window_unknown)\". Applies to ledger path mainly. For fresh reading path, start not needed (we only need reading.at). But design says \"否则：窗口内... 没有窗口且存在需要计入的行 → unknown(window_unknown)\" — the \"否则\" branch (ledger). So window_unknown only in ledger path. For fresh reading, no window needed. I'll implement window_unknown only in ledger path.\n\nOrdering of unknown reasons within a pool: if rows lack capacity → ledger_capacity_unknown; if no window → window_unknown. Which precedence? Untested. I'd check window first (structural), then capacity.\n\nNow model with multiple pools: \"任一成员池为 unknown → unknown(该原因)\". Which reason if multiple? Take first in order.\n\nNow forecast `pools` output mapping from evaluated detail.\n\nLet's also confirm the \"reset_at\" detail for pools without reset: resolveResetAt returns null/unknown. reset_in_h null.\n\nFor A-8: window has no reset_source, reset_at present → config → reset_at ISO normalized with .000Z ✓, reset_in_h = (12:00 - 10:00)/1h = 2 ✓ source config ✓. used_fraction 0.5, used_mtok = 10*0.5 = 5, start 07:00 → hours 3 → burn = 5/3 = 1.6666 → 1.667 ✓. eta: remaining 5, burn 1.667 → 5/1.667*3600000 = 2.9994h → now + ... Let's check expected 2026-11-07T12:59:57.840Z. 5/1.667 = 2.99940... hours = 10,797,840 ms? 5/1.667*3600000 = 10,797,840.4... Let's compute: 1.667*2 = 3.334; remaining 5/1.667 = 2.9994001... ×3.6e6 = 10,797,840.4 → Math.round = 10,797,840 → 10:00 + 2:59:57.840 = 12:59:57.840 ✓. Great — so burn used is the rounded 1.667 (round3), confirming eta uses rounded burn_mtok_per_hour (the field). Good.\n\nAnd exhausts_before_reset: eta 12:59:57 < 12:00? false ✓.\n\nNow `required` fields: also `tokens_per_task`. Schema requires it with object|null. We always object.\n\nAlso `burn_per_task`: cost sequence mean round3. For q-usd: costs 0.5×3 → 0.5.\n\nNow AC-015 A-2: for q-pct cases, `samples` from golden is array of objects. `samples.length` = 0 for most.\n\nCareful: `buildForecast` destructuring `samples` default: `samples` may be undefined (AC-017 A-11 passes samples). Use `samples = []`.\n\nNow `usage` unknown → treat Normal for quantile (handled) and for estimate: fallback Normal.\n\nNow write pools.mjs. Also need `assertNow` in pools (for resolveResetAt/evaluatePools) and forecast.\n\nPotential check-seams issue: pools.mjs will use `new Date(ms).toISOString()` — has argument → allowed. Also `Date.parse` is not flagged (only Date.now / new Date()). ✓\n\nLet me now check whether `lib/pools.mjs` containing the substring \"setTimeout\" etc. — no.\n\nAnother check: R-4 scans files for 'sk-', 'Bearer ', 'ghp_', 'xox', 'AKIA'. Our test files must avoid these substrings. Beware \"xox\" — unlikely. But 'sk-' could appear in... no.\n\nNow write the code.\n\npools.mjs:\n\n```js\n// Pure quota-pool normalization and remaining-capacity arithmetic.\n// No wall clock, no timers, no IO: every time value arrives as an explicit millisecond number.\n\nconst DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT = 0\nconst HOUR_MS = 3600000\n\nfunction toFiniteNumber(value) {\n  if (typeof value === 'number') return Number.isFinite(value) ? value : null\n  if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim() !== '') {\n    const parsed = Number(value)\n    return Number.isFinite(parsed) ? parsed : null\n  }\n  return null\n}\n\nfunction toMillis(value) {\n  if (typeof value === 'number') return Number.isFinite(value) ? value : null\n  if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim() !== '') {\n    const parsed = Date.parse(value)\n    return Number.isFinite(parsed) ? parsed : null\n  }\n  return null\n}\n\nfunction isoOrNull(ms) {\n  return ms === null ? null : new Date(ms).toISOString()\n}\n\nfunction requireNow(now) {\n  if (!Number.isFinite(now)) throw new TypeError('now must be a finite millisecond timestamp')\n  return now\n}\n```\n\nWait: `Number.isFinite(now)` — if now is numeric string? Design: now 是毫秒数. Require number. `Number.isFinite('0')` false → throws. Acceptance passes numbers. OK.\n\nround3 as designed.\n\nbilledTokens:\n```js\nexport function billedTokens(row, cache_read_weight = DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT) {\n  if (!row || typeof row !== 'object') return 0\n  if (typeof row.tokens === 'number' && Number.isFinite(row.tokens)) return row.tokens\n  const weight = toFiniteNumber(cache_read_weight)\n  const w = weight === null ? DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT : weight\n  const input = toFiniteNumber(row.input_tokens) ?? 0\n  const output = toFiniteNumber(row.output_tokens) ?? 0\n  const write = toFiniteNumber(row.cache_write_tokens) ?? 0\n  const read = toFiniteNumber(row.cache_read_tokens) ?? 0\n  return input + output + write + w * read\n}\n```\n\nnormalizeQuota as above. clamp helper.\n\nresolveResetAt:\n```js\nexport function resolveResetAt({ cli = null, config = null, window = null, rows = [], now } = {}) {\n  const nowMs = requireNow(now)\n  const cliMs = toMillis(cli)\n  if (cliMs !== null) return { reset_at: isoOrNull(cliMs), reset_source: 'cli' }\n  const configMs = toMillis(config)\n  if (configMs !== null) return { reset_at: isoOrNull(configMs), reset_source: 'config' }\n  const w = window && typeof window === 'object' ? window : null\n  const lengthS = w ? toFiniteNumber(w.length_s) : null\n  if (w && w.anchor === 'rolling' && lengthS !== null && lengthS > 0) {\n    const lower = nowMs - lengthS * 1000\n    let earliest = null\n    for (const row of Array.isArray(rows) ? rows : []) {\n      const at = toMillis(row && row.at)\n      if (at === null) continue\n      if (at > lower && at <= nowMs && (earliest === null || at < earliest)) earliest = at\n    }\n    if (earliest !== null) return { reset_at: isoOrNull(earliest + lengthS * 1000), reset_source: 'estimated' }\n  }\n  return { reset_at: null, reset_source: 'unknown' }\n}\n```\nCheck AC-019 estimated: now 10:00, length 3600 → lower 09:00. Rows 08:00 (excluded), 09:30, 09:10 → earliest 09:10 + 1h = 10:10 ✓.\n\nevaluatePools:\n\n```js\nfunction capacityFor(pool, model) {\n  const map = pool && pool.capacity_mtok && typeof pool.capacity_mtok === 'object' ? pool.capacity_mtok : null\n  if (!map) return null\n  const raw = map[model]\n  if (raw && typeof raw === 'object') return toFiniteNumber(raw.value)\n  return toFiniteNumber(raw)\n}\n\nfunction readingFor(pool) {\n  if (pool && pool.reading && typeof pool.reading === 'object') {\n    const value = toFiniteNumber(pool.reading.value)\n    const at = toMillis(pool.reading.at)\n    if (value !== null && at !== null) return { value, at }\n    return null\n  }\n  if (pool && pool.used_fraction && typeof pool.used_fraction === 'object') {\n    const value = toFiniteNumber(pool.used_fraction.value)\n    const at = toMillis(pool.used_fraction.at)\n    if (value !== null && at !== null) return { value, at }\n  }\n  return null\n}\n```\n\nPool window candidate derivation:\n```js\nfunction resetCandidates(pool) {\n  const window = pool && pool.window && typeof pool.window === 'object' ? pool.window : null\n  if (!window) return { window: null, cli: null, config: null }\n  const source = window.reset_source ?? null\n  if (source === 'cli') return { window, cli: window.reset_at ?? null, config: null }\n  if (source === 'config' || source === null) return { window, cli: null, config: window.reset_at ?? null }\n  return { window, cli: null, config: null }\n}\n```\nCareful: if window exists but no reset_at and no reset_source → config null → resolve returns unknown. Good.\n\nBut `resolveResetAt` uses window for rolling estimate; passing the same window with `anchor:'rolling'` works.\n\nAlso for source 'estimated'/'unknown', discard stored reset_at: pass cli/config null, but window includes reset_at — resolveResetAt ignores window.reset_at, only uses anchor/length_s. ✓\n\nPer-pool evaluation:\n\n```js\nexport function evaluatePools({ models = [], pools = [], rows = [], now, reading_ttl_s = 600, cache_read_weight = DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT } = {}) {\n  const nowMs = requireNow(now)\n  const ttl = toFiniteNumber(reading_ttl_s)\n  const ttlMs = (ttl === null ? 600 : ttl) * 1000\n  const poolList = Array.isArray(pools) ? pools : []\n  const rowList = Array.isArray(rows) ? rows : []\n  const modelList = Array.isArray(models) ? models : []\n  const states = poolList.map((pool) => poolState(pool, rowList, nowMs, ttlMs, cache_read_weight))\n  const result = {}\n  for (const model of modelList) {\n    const members = []\n    for (let i = 0; i < poolList.length; i += 1) {\n      const cap = capacityFor(poolList[i], model)\n      if (cap === null) continue\n      members.push({ pool: poolList[i], state: states[i], cap })\n    }\n    result[model] = modelResult(model, members, nowMs)\n  }\n  return result\n}\n```\n\npoolState:\n```js\nfunction poolState(pool, rows, nowMs, ttlMs, cacheReadWeight) {\n  const candidates = resetCandidates(pool)\n  const resolved = resolveResetAt({ cli: candidates.cli, config: candidates.config, window: candidates.window, rows, now: nowMs })\n  const resetMs = toMillis(resolved.reset_at)\n  const crossed = resetMs !== null && nowMs >= resetMs\n  const recheck = crossed && resolved.reset_source !== 'cli'\n  const windowStart = candidates.window ? toMillis(candidates.window.start_at) : null\n  const startMs = crossed && resolved.reset_source === 'cli' ? resetMs : windowStart\n  const reading = readingFor(pool)\n  const validReading = reading !== null && !(crossed && resolved.reset_source === 'cli' && reading.at < resetMs) && nowMs - reading.at <= ttlMs\n  ...\n}\n```\nHmm: reading validation also needs reading.at <= now? now - at could be negative if at in future → <= ttl true → fresh. Fine.\n\nCompute usage:\n```js\n  let used = null\n  let reason = null\n  const contributing = []\n  if (validReading) {\n    used = validReading.value\n    for (const row of rows) {\n      const at = toMillis(row && row.at)\n      if (at === null || at <= validReading.at || at > nowMs) continue\n      contributing.push(row)\n    }\n  } else {\n    const relevant = []\n    for (const row of rows) {\n      const at = toMillis(row && row.at)\n      if (at === null || at > nowMs) continue\n      if (startMs !== null && at < startMs) continue\n      relevant.push(row)\n    }\n    if (startMs === null && relevant.length > 0) reason = 'window_unknown'\n    else contributing.push(...relevant)\n    if (reason === null) used = 0\n  }\n```\nWait for fresh reading we add reading.value + increments.\n\nThen for each contributing row: cap = capacityFor(pool, row.model); if cap === null or cap <= 0 → reason = 'ledger_capacity_unknown' (if reason null or still); break-ish. else used += billedTokens(row, cacheReadWeight)/(cap*1e6).\n\nOrder: window_unknown takes precedence (set only if start null). Capacity check should override? Design: \"只 participate rows...\" no precedence. I'll let ledger_capacity_unknown take precedence if found, since it's about the row. Hmm: if no window AND rows lack capacity, either. I'll keep first-found: window first (don't overwrite). Then capacity only if reason null.\n\nWait but if window_unknown, we skip summing? Either way unknown.\n\nClamp: `used = used === null ? null : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, used))`.\n\nReturn state { used, reason, startMs, resetMs, resetAt: resolved.reset_at, resetSource: resolved.reset_source, recheck }.\n\nmodelResult:\n```js\nfunction modelResult(memberList, nowMs) {\n  if (memberList.length === 0) {\n    return { status: 'unknown', remaining_mtok: null, remaining_fraction: null, reason: 'capacity_unknown', pools: [] }\n  }\n  const unknownMember = memberList.find((m) => m.state.used === null)\n  // pools detail for each member\n  const details = memberList.map(({ pool, state, cap }) => detail(...))\n  if (unknownMember) return { status: 'unknown', remaining_mtok: null, remaining_fraction: null, reason: unknownMember.state.reason ?? 'capacity_unknown', pools: details }\n  ...\n}\n```\nBut details for unknown pools: remaining null.\n\nDetails:\n```js\nfunction poolDetail(pool, state, cap, nowMs) {\n  const known = state.used !== null\n  const remainingFraction = known ? 1 - state.used : null\n  return {\n    pool_id: pool.id,\n    remaining_mtok: known ? round3(cap * remainingFraction) : null,\n    remaining_fraction: known ? round3(remainingFraction) : null,\n    used_fraction: known ? state.used : null,\n    used_mtok: known ? cap * state.used : null,\n    reset_at: state.resetAt,\n    reset_in_h: state.resetMs === null ? null : Math.max(0, round3((state.resetMs - nowMs) / HOUR_MS)),\n    reset_source: state.resetSource,\n    recheck: state.recheck,\n  }\n}\n```\npool_id: pool.id may be undefined; schema requires string. Use String(pool.id ?? '')? Hmm S13. Design says pool_id. Use `pool.id ?? ''`. Fine but schema expects string; if undefined → null fails validation. Use `typeof pool.id === 'string' ? pool.id : String(pool.id ?? '')`.\n\nremaining_mtok round3: for 1.8 from b44-ledger: 2*(1-0.1)=1.8000000000000003 → round3 → 1.8 ✓.\n\nFor known model across multiple pools: remaining_mtok = round3(min over members of cap*(1-used)); remaining_fraction = round3(min of (1-used)). Design §3.5 says \"模型结果 ... `remaining_mtok: round3(min_p remaining_p)`\"; `evaluatePools` returns `{ remaining_fraction: round3(min_p (1 - used_p)) }`. Note min remaining_fraction may come from a different pool than min remaining_mtok — fine.\n\nNow remainingForModels:\n```js\nexport function remainingForModels({ models = [], pools = [], rows = [], now, reading_ttl_s = 600, cache_read_weight = DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT } = {}) {\n  const evaluated = evaluatePools({ ... })\n  const projection = {}\n  for (const model of models) {\n    const item = evaluated[model]\n    projection[model] = { status: item.status, remaining_mtok: item.remaining_mtok, reason: item.reason }\n  }\n  return projection\n}\n```\nCareful: models may be non-array → normalize.\n\nBut note: evaluatePools already only returns models requested. Iterate Object.keys(evaluated) to preserve? Better iterate models to keep order (deepStrictEqual ignores order). Use evaluated keys safer: `for (const model of Object.keys(evaluated))`.\n\nNow forecast.mjs engine.\n\nbuildForecast:\n\n```js\nexport function buildForecast({ model = '', quota = null, pools = null, rows = [], samples = [], usage = 'Normal', now, policy = null } = {}) {\n  const nowMs = requireNow(now)\n  const effective = mergePolicy(policy)\n  const poolList = Array.isArray(pools) ? pools : []\n  const sampleList = Array.isArray(samples) ? samples : []\n  ...\n}\n```\nmergePolicy:\n```js\nfunction mergePolicy(policy) {\n  const base = policy && typeof policy === '