{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b76c-6755-779d-8834-a448d1640c04","session_id":"01a1b769-9e30-7c78-9a9c-20b26d74eef6","message":{"id":"01a1b76c6755779d8834a4464ec98ebe","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait: in `poolState`, when reading is usable, `used += ...` requires `used` number. If readingUsable and no contributing rows, used = reading.value fine. If not usable and reason null, used=0. If window_unknown, used stays null but reason set. Then `if (reason === null)` capacity loop; if reason was window_unknown we skip. Good.\n\nBut bug: if `readingUsable` is false and reason becomes 'window_unknown', used remains null → good.\n\nAnother bug: `used += ...` when used is null? Only reached when reason === null; if readingUsable, used is number; else used = 0. But if reason was 'window_unknown', we skip the loop (reason !== null). Good.\n\nEdge: readingUsable true but reading.value maybe... fine.\n\nNow forecast.mjs.\n\nCareful to keep old exports exactly, add `@deprecated` comment. Must not write \"Date.now\" in comments.\n\nAlso `systemNow` count must stay exactly 2. Import + default param.\n\nLet me write the whole file.\n\nAlso `requireNow` duplicate.\n\nOne consideration: `etaExhaust` default `remaining_mtok` handling.\n\nAlso `burnMtokPerHour` destructuring when called as `burnMtokPerHour(input)` where input may be undefined.\n\nWrite now.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","_messageId":"01a1b76c6755779d8834a4464ec98ebe","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b769a1b5702aa92833dbee5b67a6","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b76c6755779d8834a4464ec98ebe","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b76c6755779d8834a4464ec